cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use electric-eye in your research, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "electric-eye: Real-Time Image Enhancement and Low-Latency Video Transport for Remotely Operated Underwater Vehicles"
abstract: >-
  electric-eye is realtime camera software for a remotely operated underwater
  vehicle, built for a BlueROV and any GNU/Linux machine. eeye takes frames
  from a camera, runs them through a chain of image-enhancement effects, and
  publishes the pilot's picture and the untouched camera frame on a
  shared-memory frame bus; hellion carries the video across the tether as
  H.264 over RTP, feeds QGroundControl, records MP4 and serves the browser
  control page.
